# One line ending in the repository, whatever the working tree was written with.
#
# The tree arrived with 16 files in CRLF and the rest in LF; without this, a
# diff of a file that was only saved by a different editor shows every line as
# changed. `text=auto` lets Git normalise to LF in the index and check out with
# the platform's ending; `eol=lf` on the text types this project owns keeps even
# that predictable, because the fonts, tests and Prettier config all assume LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never normalise, never try to diff.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.f32 binary
*.bin binary
*.hea binary
*.npy binary
